#: ../../../developer/debugging/windows-debugging.rst:3
#: f660570db9d34823a59e201443735351
msgid "Windows debugging"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/windows-debugging.rst:6
#: 043dd5d2a1de42cb9a951b611b3c2062
msgid ""
"Debugging Windows code can be tricky in a virtualized environment. The guide "
"below assumes Qubes 4.2 and Windows 7 or later VMs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/windows-debugging.rst:8
#: 72bfdb9d13694cf7b68484ad053b5627
msgid ""
"User-mode debugging is usually straightforward if it can be done on one "
"machine. Just duplicate your normal debugging environment in the VM."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/windows-debugging.rst:10
#: 2183c700e1f14f049f595332b27835e2
msgid ""
"Things get complicated if you need to perform kernel debugging or "
"troubleshoot problems that only manifest on system boot, user logoff or "
"similar. For that you need two Windows VMs: the *host* and the *target*. The "
"*host* will contain the debugger, your source code and private symbols. The "
"*target* will run the code being debugged. We will use kernel debugging over "
"network which is supported from Windows 7 onwards. The main caveat is that "
"Windows kernel supports only specific network adapters for this, and the "
"default one in Qubes won’t work."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/windows-debugging.rst:13
#: 5448f5cf31274229b184c252b47d1e02
msgid "Important note"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/windows-debugging.rst:16
#: d1acfc5f047144f7936778c172f588f3
msgid ""
"Do not install Xen network PV drivers in the target VM. Network kernel "
"debugging needs a specific type of NIC or it won’t work, the network PV "
"drivers interfere with that."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/windows-debugging.rst:18
#: 710a179e2bc3462da4cb57408769ebf9
msgid ""
"If you have kernel debugging active when the Xen PV drivers are being "
"installed, make sure to disable it before rebooting (``bcdedit /set debug "
"off``). You can re-enable debugging after the reboot. The OS won’t boot "
"otherwise. I’m not sure what’s the exact cause. I know that busparams for "
"the debugging NIC change when PV drivers are installed (see later), but even "
"changing that accordingly in the debug settings doesn’t help – so it’s best "
"to disable debug for this one reboot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/windows-debugging.rst:23
#: 400b3824bbc1461cb3a7719834d04f75
msgid "Modifying the NIC of the target VM"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/windows-debugging.rst:26
#: d3209f6653d34529b08dbf247852460c
msgid ""
"You will need to create a :doc:`custom libvirt config <core-admin:libvirt>` "
"for the target VM. The following assumes the target VM is named ``target-"
"vm``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/windows-debugging.rst:28
#: 81548b51037843b682a1da5c81c21b41
msgid ""
"Edit ``/usr/share/qubes/templates/libvirt/xen.xml`` to prepare our custom "
"config to override just the NIC part of the global template:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/windows-debugging.rst:30
#: 749820b2a8af40fda054adbda278f82c
msgid "add ``{% block network %}`` before ``{% if vm.netvm %}``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/windows-debugging.rst:32
#: 0331fa5e65ca47018664d7790919062e
msgid "add ``{% endblock %}`` after the matching ``{% endif %}``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/windows-debugging.rst:36
#: 161efb98473e4275ba11d3f72b502dd6
msgid ""
"Copy ``/usr/share/qubes/templates/libvirt/devices/net.xml`` to ``/etc/qubes/"
"templates/libvirt/xen/by-name/target-vm.xml``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/windows-debugging.rst:38
#: 47c047f898334af2b2c114411150ac4c
msgid "Add ``<model type='e1000'/>`` to the ``<interface>`` section."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/windows-debugging.rst:40
#: fccaf255480647e8bdb15c3ecd665d4a
msgid "Enclose everything within ``{% block network %}`` + ``{% endblock %}``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/windows-debugging.rst:42
#: f5539703562c4fbd93b07dc4ba243543
msgid "Add ``{% extends 'libvirt/xen.xml' %}`` at the start."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/windows-debugging.rst:44
#: 1c858a6da3cd4fbebe63a6f074f8bf30
msgid "The final ``target-vm.xml`` should look something like this:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/windows-debugging.rst:65
#: e029c2ee17d84c1a83f87bb0d3753c33
msgid ""
"Start ``target-vm`` and verify in the device manager that a “Intel PRO/1000 "
"MT” adapter is present."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/windows-debugging.rst:70
#: 04451681f11340f1a5357c587d7174bd
msgid "Host and target preparation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/windows-debugging.rst:73
#: cb33a895708141b6875dffccbb92ebfe
msgid ""
"On ``host-vm`` you will need WinDbg, which is a part of the `Windows SDK "
"<https://developer.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/downloads/windows-sdk/>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/windows-debugging.rst:75
#: db8c6b18ad9845b89c40bd01592bfb3f
msgid "Copy the ``Debuggers`` directory from Windows SDK to ``target-vm``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/windows-debugging.rst:77
#: 3f8f643ff198430c92c19a148b7f87a8
msgid ""
"In both ``host-vm`` and ``target-vm`` switch the windows network to private "
"(it tends to be public by default)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/windows-debugging.rst:79
#: 40022eb03b7847709bbe78f3e93c19f2
msgid ""
"Either turn off the windows firewall or enable all ICMP-in rules in both VMs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/windows-debugging.rst:81
#: bda47416f611461587bfd88fb2fb85a9
msgid ""
"In ``firewall-vm`` edit ``/rw/config/qubes-firewall-user-script`` to connect "
"both Windows VMs, add:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/windows-debugging.rst:83
#: b50e8d3a936340ce974365cc803c7475
msgid "``iptables -I FORWARD 2 -s <target-vm-ip> -d <host-vm-ip> -j ACCEPT``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/windows-debugging.rst:85
#: e47c8fa864d641b3a3910acbbb50201c
msgid "``iptables -I FORWARD 2 -s <host-vm-ip> -d <target-vm-ip> -j ACCEPT``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/windows-debugging.rst:87
#: d23cb976d13e4632a5e2e687c6f4ee17
msgid ""
"run ``/rw/config/qubes-firewall-user-script`` so the changes take effect "
"immediately"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/windows-debugging.rst:91
#: d120d4e26b3c4702a40f014a53ce8114
msgid "Make sure both VMs can ping each other."
msgstr ""

